          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have just been diagnosed with type 2 diabetes. What does the diagnosis mean, what does guidance describe as first-line therapy, and which code covers it?",
          "answer": "**What the diagnosis means:** The retrieved material does not explain type 2 diabetes clinically. Your clinician can explain what it means for your body and your daily life.\n\n**First-line therapy:** The search did not find any guidance on first-line treatment for type 2 diabetes, so I can't tell you what guidance describes. The results were about other conditions, including hypertension, anxiety, urinary tract infection and insomnia. The hypertension guidance (*Hypertension: when treatment starts and which options are first-line*) mentions diabetes only as a reason blood pressure treatment may start sooner. It does not cover diabetes treatment. Please ask your clinician which treatment plan fits you.\n\n**Code:** Type 2 diabetes mellitus is **E11** in ICD-10-CM, Chapter 4 (endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases), according to *Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories*. Taking insulin does not change the code; it is recorded as a separate status code.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
